  <entry>
    <title>Why I&apos;m Grateful Today</title>
    <id>https://lzon.ca/posts/blog/lzon/</id>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://lzon.ca/posts/blog/lzon/"/>
    <category term="blog" label="Blog" scheme="https://lzon.ca/posts/blog/"/>
    <published>2025-12-23T12:00:00Z</published>
    <updated>2025-12-23T12:00:00Z</updated>
    <author><name>Lzon</name></author>
    <content type="html" xml:base="https://lzon.ca/posts/blog/lzon/">&lt;p&gt;Today I am grateful for this website, &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://lzon.ca&quot;&gt;lzon.ca&lt;/a&gt;. I started building it about a week ago, and so far I am quite satisfied with it, at a technical level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I’m using the &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://getzola.org&quot;&gt;Zola&lt;/a&gt; static site generator. I started from scratch, without a template. I wanted to improve my web development skill, and I wanted a challenge. There was a moment on day one in which I literally had an empty index.html file loaded in my text editor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The name is a contraction of the word “Lauzon”, pronounced “loh-zawn”. It’s the name of a lake near &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener external&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blind_River,_Ontario&quot;&gt;Blind River, Ontario&lt;/a&gt;. My Mom was born there and otherwise it is a very nice little town, in a part of the province that I love. The domain was also surprising inexpensive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I think the design of the site is nice so far, and I’ve already learned a few new things related to web development and design:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A new trick for addressing FOUC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How to create advanced CSS selectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New ways to use CSS variables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I don’t know now how frequently I will publish content to this site. At the very least it can be a place to publish my rambles, when I feel compelled. Either way, I am satisfied with what this is right now.&lt;/p&gt;

</content>
